/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  thermoPhysPropDict (v2) -- gamma-phi, ideal liquid (gamma = 1, DECLARED),
  SRK vapour.

  The column runs at 16 bar.  There the vapour is not ideal: the 2026-11-07
  audit (C239) measured phi of the light key about 21 % below 1, so an
  ideal-gas vapour misprices both K and the latent heats.  The vapour is
  therefore SRK (kij = 0, announced -- hydrocarbon pairs, no interaction
  data declared).  The pure-liquid reference carries phi_sat and Poynting.
  The MESH iterates visit temperatures above the critical temperature of
  propane (369.8 K) and butane (425.1 K), where a saturated vapour does not
  exist: the reference factor is HELD at its value at 0.99 Tc (continuous
  in T, announced once per component) instead of jumping to 1.

  The column starts from the converged profile of its own ideal-vapour
  version (0/internalStates/radfrac, a declared SEED, not an answer): the
  full-MESH Newton from the built-in linear start overshoots to thousands
  of kelvin on this four-component 30-stage column and its line search
  stalls (|F| = 8.1 after 51 iterations); from the seed it converges in 4.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

recordType    thermophysicalPropertySystem;
schemaVersion 2;

components       ( propane  nButane  nPentane  nHexane );

equilibrium
{
    formulation gammaPhi;

    liquid
    {
        activityModel ideal;
        standardState pureLiquid;
    }

    vapour
    {
        fugacityModel SRK;
    }
}
